The problem was in [38;5;10mtranslated_rust/Cargo.toml[0m. The [38;5;10m[lib][0m section didn't specify a [38;5;10mname[0m, so Cargo defaulted to the package name [38;5;10mprf_addr[0m, producing [38;5;10mlibprf_addr.so[0m. However, the test runner harness was configured with [38;5;10mlibrary: "blake"[0m, meaning it tried to load [38;5;10mlibblake.so[0m — which didn't exist.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The fix was a single line addition to [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mtoml
[0m[38;5;10m[lib]
name = "blake"        # ← added this line
